  "description": "<p>The Rug Mine's vision is to deliver a piece of authentic art, history, and culture into people&rsquo;s homes everywhere. &nbsp;To achieve this, its mission is to help clients select a beautiful, durable, and high-quality Afghan rug that will last as an heirloom over generations. &nbsp;Whether it&rsquo;s toddlers learning to crawl or families coming together for board game nights, The Rug Mine&rsquo;s quality, durable rugs serve as canvases for its clients&rsquo; memories. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The Rug Mine is driven by a desire to make all people feel good in their spaces: cozy, comfortable, and creative. &nbsp;For this reason, each rug is made by seasoned Afghan artisans (mostly women) who, like Nargis, are dedicated to empowering women and crafting fair trade, sustainable rugs. &nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>The Rug Mine is a woman-and-minority-owned business founded in June 2020 that sells handmade rugs from Afghanistan. &nbsp;Its sole owner, Nargis Habib, is the first and only Afghan woman to source and sell Afghan rugs exclusively online to the global market. &nbsp;She is also the only Afghan retailer to invest profits into fair trade and sustainability efforts in Afghanistan.</p>",
